  "about": "A touchscreen: what it registers with (beside an e-paper screen's registration, the same route) and is answered, what GET /api/devices/config answers before it is paired (the pairing value: its config with the code to show and its style's and display's defaults) and after, and what it saves with PUT /api/devices/config from its own settings panel (`save`: the whole config as it got it, its skin and sleep changed, read-only fields and all). and what GET /api/devices/spotify/token answers it once paired (`spotify_token`: an access token for its owner's Spotify). The touchscreen's tests check its client against these, and the broker's tests its routes. An e-paper screen's config is config_store.json's. The store contract's canonical example (countdown-api's countdown_api/fixtures), which every consumer's tests read: change it there.",
